[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 17:15] Now bring it together. What's your recommendation to the CEO?

[candidate · 18:45] My recommendation: Brew & Bean should raise menu prices, and pair that with a procurement program to stabilize input costs.

The root cause is clear. COGS went from 42% to 58% of revenue, which is 16 of the 18 points of margin lost. Beans are up 40% and other inputs up 37.5% — blended, about 38% input inflation — while menu prices have not moved in two years. When I run those increases through the old cost base, I land exactly on today's 58%. So this is entirely unpassed-through inflation, not waste, mix, or operational failure.

Supporting moves: forward-contract or hedge beans, consolidate vendors across 200 stores for scale, and nudge mix toward lower-input-cost drinks.

Risks: a 38% price increase in one step would likely cost volume, so I'd phase it and test elasticity in a few markets first. There's also competitive risk if peers haven't raised prices.

Next steps: run a price test in 10–20 stores, and get the supplier contract terms to size negotiating room.
